 75CU c  Compiled (unevaluated) dataset from 2020De21:                          
 75CU c  Nature Physics 16, 620 (2020)                                          
 75CU c  Compiled by E.A. McCutchan (NNDC,BNL) July 9, 2020                     
 75CU c  {+75}Cu isotope was produced by bombarding {+238}U target              
 75CU2c  with neutrons produced by impinging a 1.4 GeV proton beam              
 75CU3c  on a neutron converter at the CERN-ISOLDE facility.                    
 75CU4c  Cu isotopes were selectively ionized by the RILIS laser ion source,    
 75CU5c  accelerated to 30 keV for mass separation with high-resolution mass    
 75CU6c  separator, and injected into ISCOOL gas-filled linear Paul trap.       
 75CU7c  Measured isotope shift with respect to {+65}Cu using collinear         
 75CU8c  resonance ionization spectroscopy.                                     
 75CU  L 0.0         5/2                                                        
